    <h2>What Is the Royal Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Royal Reese's® Blizzard takes the standard <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's PB Cup Blizzard</a> — already one of the highest-calorie Blizzards — and injects a warm peanut butter-filled center into the cup. When you reach the middle, you hit a pocket of warm, rich peanut butter that amplifies the flavor intensity significantly. This is the richest Blizzard on the entire year-round menu.</p>
  <p>Browse all Blizzards and 2026 prices on <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Standard Reese's vs. Royal Reese's</h2>
  <p>The standard <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's® Blizzard</a> costs $3.49 Mini (Mini). The Royal Reese's is $3.99 Mini — a $0.50 upgrade. The Royal version adds a warm peanut butter-filled center that creates a temperature and flavor burst at the core of the cup. For peanut butter fans, this upgrade is well worth it. For first-timers to the Reese's Blizzard, start with the standard version to establish the baseline before deciding on the Royal upgrade.</p>
  <h2>Calorie Note</h2>
  <p>At approximately 1,280 cal for the Large, the Royal Reese's is the highest-calorie Blizzard on the DQ menu. The Small at 620 cal is the recommended size for most guests.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Royal Reese's® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>620</td><td>PB cup pieces + PB center — richest</td></tr><tr><td>Standard Reese's® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>600</td><td>PB cup pieces only</td></tr><tr><td>Royal Oreo® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>490</td><td>Oreo + fudge center</td></tr><tr><td>Butterfinger® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>470</td><td>Lightest PB option</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.99) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.99) at 620 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

